# `view_errors.post`

Record a view runtime error reported by the browser.

**Policy** — read (C0, safe). Capability `ship.views.write`.

## Arguments

| name | type |
|------|------|
| `view` | `string` |
| `url` | `string` |
| `kind` | `string` |
| `message` | `string` |
| `stack` | `string` |
| `filename` | `string` |
| `line` | `number` |
| `column` | `number` |
| `detail_json` | `string` |
| `user_agent` | `string` |
| `timestamp_client` | `string` |

## Returns

`PostViewErrorResponse` (JSON).

| field | type |
|-------|------|
| `id` | `number` |
| `accepted` | `bool` |

## Invoke

```
ship ops call view_errors.post --json '{ "view": "", "url": "", "kind": "", "message": "", "stack": "", "filename": "", "line": 0, "column": 0, "detail_json": "", "user_agent": "", "timestamp_client": "" }'
```

Kind: read.

## Example response

```json
{
  "id": 1,
  "accepted": true
}
```
